<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply cut in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply cut in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Bank withdrew liquidity from the money market in the week to Nov 25 due to a fall in bank notes in circulation and a reduction in the Belgian state's deposits with the bank.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   414.28 (+    0.31)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  13.05 (+    1.58)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  3.23 (+    0.16)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   24.81 (+/-  0.00)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 106.90 (-    3.07)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   449.00 (-    0.75)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>NOTE: the central bank said revenues from its issue of 230 billion francs of certificates of deposits were being used to offset losses on the bank's external assets and to create provisions for payment defaults which could result from international agreements.</p>
<p>The above operations had no effect on money market liquidity, the bank said.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
